// CROWN — a declared negation on a higher-order fn is a promise about EVERY
// call, the parameter's row included: `run` may call `f`, so `!E` constrains
// what callers pass. Boot admitted the free parameter row at the gate and
// accepted a caller passing an E-performing function
// (Hβ.infer.declared-row-vacuous-against-a-free-body-row). Expect
// E_EffectMismatch.
effect E { op() -> Int }
fn run(f) with !E = f()
fn caller() = run(() => op())
fn main() = 0
